 ## Overview
-Particle Rendering via Grid Bucketing renders particles as spheres by mapping them to a spatial grid to accelerate ray-sphere intersection tests [S1]. It differs from [Ray Marching Particle Grid Traversal](5182-ray-marching-particle-grid-traversal.md) by explicitly iterating over particle lists stored in grid buckets rather than marching through a voxel grid to find hits, and from [2D Projection 1D Lookup Particle Cache](8958-2d-projection-1d-lookup-particle-cache.md) by relying on 3D spatial hashing rather than 2D screen-space caching.
